    fix(cli): DF-H3-3 - install accepts --name as an alias for the positional NAME
    
    Addresses DF-H3-3
    
    `hermes-h3 install --name X --endpoint URL` died with "No such option
    '--name'" and the plugin surface `hermes h3 install --name X --endpoint
    URL` died with argparse's "unrecognized arguments: --name": NAME was a
    required positional while the help text, the docs, and verify's own
    --harness/-h alias all advertised the flag idiom, so a dogfood judge and
    real users guessed the flag form.
    
    Mirror verify's precedent on both entry points (src/h3_shim/cli.py and
    the h3/ plugin mirror): NAME becomes an optional positional with a
    --name alias, resolved once as `name if name is not None else name_opt`,
    raising a loud click.UsageError (exit 2) when neither is given so no
    unnamed entry can ever be installed.  The positional form behaves
    byte-identically to before and wins when both are given; the plugin
    rebuilds --name into the positional argv (an unset --name is omitted, so
    click still reports the missing name).
    
    --endpoint/--transport/--timeout-ms/--set-default semantics and
    transport validation are untouched.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
